Third-party data
----------------

The timetable, station, fare and route-shape data in
SEPTACommute/MetroKit/Data/GeneratedSEPTAData.swift and
SEPTACommute/Resources/SEPTAExtended.txt is derived from the
Southeastern Pennsylvania Transportation Authority's published GTFS feed:

    https://github.com/septadev/GTFS

That data is SEPTA's, not the author's, and the copyright notice above does not
extend to it. It is used under SEPTA's developer licence:

    https://www.septa.org/license-agreement/

SEPTA's name, the names of its lines and routes, and its line colours are used
here to describe its services. This project is not affiliated with, endorsed by,
or supported by SEPTA.

Live bike-share availability comes from Indego's public GBFS feed
(https://gbfs.bcycle.com/bcycle_indego/), and Indego's published prices are
quoted to estimate ride costs. Indego is the City of Philadelphia's bike-share
system, operated by Bicycle Transit Systems on the BCycle platform. That data
is theirs, not the author's. This project is not affiliated with, endorsed by,
or supported by Indego, the City of Philadelphia, Bicycle Transit Systems or
BCycle.

Maps and walking and cycling directions are provided by Apple Maps. Elevation
data comes from Open-Meteo (https://open-meteo.com).
Drive routes and toll costs, when the user supplies a HERE key, come from HERE
Technologies' Routing API (https://www.here.com).
